<title>SWITZERLAND: Swiss govt sets terms on new 20-year federal bond.</title>
<headline>Swiss govt sets terms on new 20-year federal bond.</headline>
<dateline>BERNE 1997-05-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following issue was announced by the Swiss Federal Treasury, to yield 4.326 percent. It was priced at 99.00.</p>
<p>BORROWER - Swiss Government</p>
<p> AMT   = 228 MLN CHF* COUPON    = 4.25     MATURITY=05.JUN.17</p>
<p> TYPE  =fixed-rate    ISS PRICE = 99.00    PAY DATE=  05.JUN.97</p>
<p>The government also reserved a further 200 million Swiss</p>
<p>francs for its own accounts.</p>
<p>-- Zurich Editorial, +41 1 631 7340</p>
</text>
